<title>USA: UPS says final offer remains final.</title>
<headline>UPS says final offer remains final.</headline>
<dateline>ATLANTA 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Parcel Service said Tuesday it was ready to honor a request from Labor Secretary Alexis Herman to return to the bargaining table, but added that its &quot;last, best and final&quot; offer would not change.</p>
<p>&quot;We are ready to go back to the table. But our position hasn't changed about our offer. We've made our last, best and final offer,&quot; UPS spokesman Norman Black said.</p>
<p>&quot;It's not being compromised. It hasn't been changed. And we still believe our employees have a right to consider it.&quot;</p>
<p>((Atlanta Bureau -- 404-870-7340))</p>
